# Runtime performance: Fai, Rust and OCaml

**Measured:** 2026-10-12 · **Source:** [`aaaaaaaaaaaa`](https://github.com/example/fai/tree/aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa) · [Data and reproducibility](https://example.test/evidence)

Time taken by native compiled programs after startup. Program startup and shutdown are reported separately below.

**Lower ratios favor Fai.** Each ratio is Fai ÷ the comparison language: **0.80× means 20% less time**; **1.20× means 20% more**.

[Shared algorithms](#shared-algorithms) · [Standard-library workloads](#standard-library-workloads) · [Measurement details](#measurement-details)

## Shared algorithms

The same algorithms and logical data structures in all three languages. Compiler optimizations and runtime representations may differ.

**Coverage:** 33 benchmarks · 66 input cases.

### Summary — all measured inputs

| Compared with | Cases used | Geometric mean | Arithmetic mean | 90th percentile |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Rust | 66 / 66 | 0.500× | 0.500× | 0.500× |
| OCaml | 66 / 66 | 0.400× | 0.400× | 0.400× |

Each included case has equal weight. The geometric mean summarizes multiplicative ratios; the arithmetic mean averages them directly. The 90th percentile is the ratio at or below which 90% of the included cases fall.
